## After successful initialization, run:
mkdir -p $HOME/.kube

## Copy the admin configuration:
sudo cp -i /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf $HOME/.kube/config

## Change ownership:
sudo chown $(id -u):$(id -g) $HOME/.kube/config

Verify:
kubectl get nodes

## Initially, the Master may show:
NAME          STATUS     ROLES           AGE
kube-master   NotReady   control-plane   2m

Now, why is the Master NotReady?
Because we have not installed the CNI network plugin yet.
